<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerhard III, Count of Holstein-Rendsburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1292–1340</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Gerhard the Great, Gerhard the Bald</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerhard III (c. 1292–1340), called the Great or the Bald, was Count of Holstein-Rendsburg and the dominant power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> during the interregnum of 1332–1340. After defeating King Christopher II he held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a> and Funen in pledge and controlled the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> as guardian of its young duke. He was murdered at Randers in 1340 by the Jutish nobleman Niels Ebbesen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerhard-iii-count-of-holstein-rendsburg.jpg" alt="Gerhard III, Count of Holstein-Rendsburg" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thiset's book contains contributions from a number of artists. This illustration (seal no. 164) was drawn by Emmery R... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grevgerhardssegl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
